# Landing page experiment — verification + PR/merge gate

Applies when implementing or touching the **landing page experiment** (`/`, `LandingStudio`, marquee / ascii / moodboard / doors).

After implementing the landing page experiment, **do not stop at “done”**.

You must verify, capture screenshots, and prepare a PR/merge recommendation.

Hard rule:

```txt
no screenshots = no merge recommendation.
```

Do not invent screenshots. If screenshots cannot be captured, say why and provide an exact manual checklist — still **no merge recommendation**.

## 1. Implementation verification

Verify the landing page actually changed at runtime.

Check:

- `/` route renders the new landing
- top marquee is visible
- ascii/generative object is visible
- moodboard is visible
- doors/entry links are visible and clickable
- mobile layout is usable
- no horizontal overflow
- existing routes still work

## 2. Screenshots required

Capture **real** screenshots from local dev server or deploy preview.

Required screenshots:

- `landing-desktop.png`
- `landing-mobile-390.png`
- `landing-mobile-430.png`
- `landing-marquee.png`
- `landing-ascii-object.png`
- `landing-moodboard.png`
- `landing-doors.png`

If visual bugs exist, also capture:

- `landing-bug-[issue].png`

## 3. Interaction checks

Actually click/test:

- marquee visible and not blocking content
- each door link works:
  - two lines / daily
  - sound lab
  - book club
  - watch/listening
  - tools
  - updates
- hover/focus states if desktop
- mobile tap targets
- no horizontal scroll on 390px viewport

## 4. Checks to run

Run available project checks:

- build
- typecheck if available
- lint or scoped lint
- any route/screenshot QA script if available

Report exact commands and results. Do not claim checks passed if not run.

## 5. PR / merge output

Prepare a final report in this format:

### summary

what changed.

### files changed

exact files and purpose.

### runtime proof

route | expected | observed | screenshot

### screenshots

filename | route | viewport | what it proves

### interaction QA

link/control | action | observed result | pass/fail

### checks run

command | result | notes

### blockers

hard blockers before merge.

### non-blocking polish

visual issues that can wait.

### merge recommendation

choose one:

- open PR
- merge after small fixes
- do not merge
- split PR

Do **not** recommend merge unless:

- screenshots exist
- `/` route works
- doors links work
- mobile 390px has no horizontal overflow
- build passes or failure is explained and unrelated

### PR title

short title.

### PR description

include:

- what changed
- screenshots attached
- checks run
- known limitations
- mobile status
